# Line endings and binary handling.
#
# Without this file, a contributor whose git has core.autocrlf=true gets a CRLF
# working tree while the repository stores LF. Everything still commits
# correctly, so `git status` stays clean — but gofmt reports every Go file as
# unformatted, and `golangci-lint run` fails locally on code that is perfectly
# fine in CI. A lint gate that fails for a reason unrelated to the code is a
# gate people learn to ignore, which makes it worse than no gate at all.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` means: git decides what is text, and every text file is LF
# in the repository AND in the working tree, on every platform. The extensions
# below are then listed explicitly, so nothing important depends on git's
# guess.
#
# Anything binary is marked so, because letting eol conversion near a font or
# an image corrupts it silently.

* text=auto eol=lf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Source
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.go        text eol=lf
*.ts        text eol=lf
*.tsx       text eol=lf
*.js        text eol=lf
*.mjs       text eol=lf
*.css       text eol=lf
*.html      text eol=lf
*.sql       text eol=lf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Data and configuration
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.json      text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.md        text eol=lf
*.mod       text eol=lf
*.sum       text eol=lf

# Repository control files. M0 shipped a UTF-16 .gitignore that git could not
# read, so every rule in it silently did nothing; these are pinned for the same
# reason the encoding rule exists.
.gitignore      text eol=lf
.gitattributes  text eol=lf
.dockerignore   text eol=lf
.env.example    text eol=lf

# Extensionless files git would otherwise have to guess about.
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
Makefile    text eol=lf
LICENSE     text eol=lf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Binary — never touched by eol conversion, never diffed as text
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.woff2     binary
*.woff      binary
*.ttf       binary
*.otf       binary
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.jpeg      binary
*.gif       binary
*.webp      binary
*.ico       binary
*.pdf       binary

# SVG is text and benefits from diffing, unlike the raster formats above.
*.svg       text eol=lf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated. Still LF, but collapsed in diffs and excluded from language stats
# so a lock file does not drown a review.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
web/package-lock.json   text eol=lf linguist-generated=true
go.sum                  text eol=lf linguist-generated=true
tools/go.sum            text eol=lf linguist-generated=true
internal/store/*.sql.go text eol=lf linguist-generated=true
internal/store/models.go   text eol=lf linguist-generated=true
internal/store/querier.go  text eol=lf linguist-generated=true
internal/store/db.go       text eol=lf linguist-generated=true
